WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.980 --> 00:00:11.400
80. Formerly taboo entertainment. People's ideas about religion, clothes, money, and

2
00:00:11.400 --> 00:00:17.840
government change over the years. So do our ideas about entertainment. Some pastimes that

3
00:00:17.840 --> 00:00:23.920
we call innocent fun used to be thought of as dangerous or evil. Take playing cards,

4
00:00:23.920 --> 00:00:31.120
for example. Playing cards were first invented in India or China and then spread to Europe.

5
00:00:31.120 --> 00:00:38.040
Over time, they became the popular entertainment they are today. Many families play cards together,

6
00:00:38.040 --> 00:00:43.460
and playing cards is seen as a fun activity for parents and children. But at first, many

7
00:00:43.460 --> 00:00:48.800
Christians believed that it was a wicked game. They thought that the cards had evil powers

8
00:00:48.800 --> 00:00:55.780
that went against God. In medieval Europe, cards and dice were banned in many places.

9
00:00:55.780 --> 00:01:02.420
It was only in the 1850s that many children began to play card games. Do you like to read?

10
00:01:02.420 --> 00:01:08.980
Do you read novels? Reading novels is another activity that people used to think was wrong.

11
00:01:08.980 --> 00:01:14.180
In many parts of the Western world, novels were thought to be too exciting. People thought

12
00:01:14.180 --> 00:01:19.700
they must be bad for our health. Many people read novels in secret because they didn't

13
00:01:19.700 --> 00:01:26.660
want to be caught doing something so immoral. What about watching a play? A few centuries ago

14
00:01:26.660 --> 00:01:33.100
in Europe, people thought watching plays could be dangerous. Plays were considered lying, which was

15
00:01:33.100 --> 00:01:39.960
wrong. Some people believed that plays, like novels, were too exciting. This excitement was

16
00:01:39.960 --> 00:01:45.780
especially bad for women, they thought. Until after Shakespeare's time, going to see a play

17
00:01:45.780 --> 00:01:53.020
was taboo for many people. Soon, you'll read a book, go to a movie or play, or play cards with

18
00:01:53.020 --> 00:01:59.260
your friends and family. When you do, remember that a few hundred years ago, those activities

19
00:01:59.260 --> 00:02:01.820
might have gotten you in big trouble.
